## 6. Docs location and how they're enforced

**Docs live in** `/Users/bogac/dev/forgejo/AeroSpace/docs/aerospace-<command-name>.adoc`, one file per command, plus a stanza in `/Users/bogac/dev/forgejo/AeroSpace/docs/commands.adoc`. Shared include fragments are in `/Users/bogac/dev/forgejo/AeroSpace/docs/util/`: `man-attributes.adoc`, `man-footer.adoc`, `conditional-options-header.adoc`, `conditional-arguments-header.adoc`, `conditional-exit-code-header.adoc`, `conditional-examples-header.adoc`, `conditional-operators-header.adoc`, `conditional-interpolation-variables-header.adoc`, `conditional-output-format-header.adoc`, `window-id-flag-desc.adoc`, `workspace-flag-desc.adoc`, `monitor-option.adoc`, `all-monitors-option.adoc`, `header.adoc`, `site-attributes.adoc`.

**Is there a Swift test validating docs against command definitions? No.** I read every file under `Sources/AppBundleTests/` (49 files). Nothing iterates `CmdKind.allCases` against `docs/`. The only tests touching `docs/` are in `/Users/bogac/dev/forgejo/AeroSpace/Sources/AppBundleTests/config/ConfigTest.swift`:

```swift
let toml = try! String(contentsOf: projectRoot.appending(component: "docs/config-examples/i3-like-config-example.toml"), encoding: .utf8)
...
let toml = try! String(contentsOf: projectRoot.appending(component: "docs/config-examples/default-config.toml"), encoding: .utf8)
